ProjectE Integration

Purpose

ProjectE is a post-endgame resource transmutation system.

It must not function as an early-game convenience mod or as an alternative progression path.

ProjectE should only become available after the player has completed the main technological progression and established an extreme industrial infrastructure.

ProjectE should represent the transition from conventional industrial production into post-endgame resource manipulation.

Role in the Pack

ProjectE is responsible for:

Resource transmutation

EMC-based resource management

Extreme resource automation

Post-endgame production

Large-scale resource compression

Ultimate resource generation

ProjectE should provide capabilities that are intentionally beyond normal industrial technology.

ProjectE Unlock

ProjectE must remain locked during the main progression.

The player should only gain access after reaching the post-endgame stage.

The exact unlock requirement should require substantial completion of:

UHV progression

Advanced industrial infrastructure

Advanced automation

Cross-mod production

Exploration

Magic progression

Apotheosis progression

The final unlock should require the player to demonstrate mastery of the pack rather than simply reaching a single technological tier.

Ultimate Transmutation Core

The Ultimate Transmutation Core is the primary unlock item for ProjectE.

It should function as the main progression gate for the ProjectE system.

The recipe should require components from multiple major progression systems.

Possible requirements include:

GregTech materials

Modern Industrialization materials

Mekanism materials

AE2 components

Create components

Magical resources

Exploration resources

Rare endgame materials

The Ultimate Transmutation Core should be one of the most expensive and complex crafting objectives in the pack.

GregTech Integration

GregTech should provide a significant portion of the infrastructure required to unlock ProjectE.

UHV-level materials and components should be relevant to the Ultimate Transmutation Core.

ProjectE should require the player to complete the conventional industrial progression before transmutation becomes available.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization should contribute advanced materials, processing, or components to the ProjectE unlock.

MI should be integrated into the construction of post-endgame infrastructure.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism should contribute advanced chemical processing and specialized industrial components.

Its late-game systems may be required for materials used in ProjectE infrastructure.

Applied Energistics 2 Integration

AE2 should provide the logistics infrastructure necessary for large-scale ProjectE automation.

Advanced ME systems may be required for ProjectE production networks.

ProjectE should not replace AE2.

Instead, ProjectE and AE2 should work together to create extremely large automated resource systems.

Create Integration

Create should contribute specialized mechanical components and infrastructure.

Create logistics may be used to transport materials involved in ProjectE production.

Create should remain useful even after ProjectE is unlocked.

Exploration Integration

ProjectE should require rare resources obtained through exploration.

Certain resources may only be obtainable from:

Rare structures

Difficult dimensions

Boss encounters

Dangerous biomes

Rare world generation

Exploration should therefore remain relevant even after the player reaches the post-endgame.

Magic Integration

Advanced magical resources should contribute to the ProjectE unlock.

Magical progression should be substantially developed before ProjectE becomes available.

Magic should provide unique materials or components that cannot simply be replaced by industrial resources.

Apotheosis Integration

Apotheosis may contribute rare boss materials or advanced equipment requirements to the ProjectE unlock.

The player should have progressed deeply into the Apotheosis system before gaining full ProjectE access.

EMC Progression

ProjectE should have its own progression after the initial unlock.

Unlocking ProjectE should not immediately provide unlimited access to every resource.

The player should progressively gain access to more powerful EMC systems.

Early Post-Endgame ProjectE

Initial ProjectE access should provide basic transmutation capabilities.

The player should be able to experiment with EMC while still requiring substantial infrastructure for large-scale production.

Advanced ProjectE

Advanced ProjectE systems should introduce:

Higher EMC generation

More efficient transmutation

Advanced collectors

Energy Condensers

Large-scale resource production

Automated resource conversion

Post-endgame storage and processing

Each stage should require additional progression.

EMC Generation

EMC generation must be carefully controlled.

The pack should prevent players from creating trivial infinite-EMC loops.

High-value EMC generation should require:

Rare resources

Advanced machines

Large power infrastructure

Complex automation

Post-endgame components

EMC values should be balanced around the progression of the entire pack.

Energy Condensers

Energy Condensers should be heavily gated.

Advanced Energy Condensers should require significant post-endgame infrastructure.

Their recipes should require components from multiple technological systems.

Energy Condensers should represent a major ProjectE milestone rather than an ordinary crafting recipe.

Transmutation Progression

Transmutation should progressively expand.

Early ProjectE should provide limited transmutation.

Advanced ProjectE should provide broader resource access.

The highest level of transmutation should require completion of major post-endgame objectives.

Transmutation should remain expensive enough that progression through ProjectE still feels meaningful.

EMC Values

EMC values must be balanced carefully.

The pack should avoid assigning excessive EMC values to common resources.

Rare progression materials should have carefully controlled EMC values.

Endgame materials should not automatically become infinite resources immediately after ProjectE is unlocked.

EMC should reflect the progression value of resources.

ProjectE Automation

ProjectE automation should become one of the major post-endgame automation systems.

Advanced automation may combine:

ProjectE

AE2

GregTech

Modern Industrialization

Mekanism

Create

Large-scale power generation

The goal is to allow the player to build enormous automated resource production systems.

Progression Gates

ProjectE progression should contain multiple gates.

Possible gates include:

Ultimate Transmutation Core

Advanced EMC generation

Energy Condensers

High-tier transmutation

Rare resources

Post-endgame power infrastructure

Advanced automation

Cross-mod components

Each gate should represent a meaningful achievement.

ProjectE Quests

ProjectE should have its own quest chapter.

The chapter should introduce:

ProjectE mechanics

EMC

The Ultimate Transmutation Core

Initial transmutation

EMC generation

Energy Condensers

Advanced transmutation

Post-endgame automation

Final ProjectE objectives

Quests should guide the player without giving away the entire system immediately.

GuideME Integration

GuideME should document:

EMC mechanics

Transmutation

EMC generation

Energy Condensers

Progression gates

EMC values

Automation

Advanced ProjectE systems

The handbook should clearly explain that ProjectE is a post-endgame system.

Post-Endgame Progression

ProjectE should continue progressing after the initial unlock.

The player should gradually move from basic transmutation toward massive automated resource production.

Later ProjectE objectives should require increasingly advanced infrastructure.

ProjectE should eventually interact with Avaritia and other final progression systems.

Final ProjectE Milestone

The final ProjectE milestone should represent complete mastery of the transmutation system.

Possible requirements include:

Maximum transmutation progression

Extreme EMC generation

Fully automated resource production

Advanced Energy Condensers

Large-scale AE2 integration

Massive power infrastructure

Completion of major post-endgame objectives

The final ProjectE milestone should be one of the major achievements of the pack.

Progression Integrity

ProjectE must never bypass the progression that precedes its unlock.

Before ProjectE:

Resources must be obtained through normal progression.

Machines must be built normally.

Power must be generated normally.

Materials must be processed normally.

Exploration must remain relevant.

After ProjectE:

Transmutation becomes available as a reward for completing the progression rather than a replacement for it.

Final Goal

ProjectE should feel like the player has finally earned the ability to manipulate resources at an absurd scale.

It should not make the rest of the pack meaningless.

Instead, ProjectE should transform the enormous infrastructure built throughout the progression into the foundation for an even larger post-endgame.

The player should move from producing resources manually, to automating them industrially, and finally to manipulating them through EMC at an extreme scale.
